WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.850
NOSHASHI is built for institutions.

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:08.380
Here is how it helps six kinds of team, and the controls an organisation gets around them.

3
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.346
A treasury team holding XRP needs its year-end value to stand up to the auditor.

4
00:00:15.346 --> 00:00:21.534
Funded depth, stamped with a ledger index, is evidence of what the market could really absorb.

5
00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:24.693
Control Surface shows who can move the treasury.

6
00:00:25.143 --> 00:00:31.513
A compliance officer approving a new token needs to know whether the issuer can freeze it or claw it back.

7
00:00:31.513 --> 00:00:38.903
The Authority screen answers in one reading, and the Verification gate runs a settlement through the organisation's policy.

8
00:00:39.353 --> 00:00:44.556
A trading desk needs to know whether it could exit at size before it takes the position.

9
00:00:44.556 --> 00:00:49.167
The Order Book and Exposure screens show the funded depth, not the listed one.

10
00:00:49.617 --> 00:00:54.118
A payments company needs to credit what really arrived, to the right customer.

11
00:00:54.118 --> 00:00:57.062
Settlement shows the delivered amount and the flag.

12
00:00:57.512 --> 00:01:01.372
An issuer wants to show buyers exactly what they are exposed to.

13
00:01:01.372 --> 00:01:05.533
It can share a Passport, or a link to its free authority certificate.

14
00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:12.853
And an auditor can recompute every receipt's digest, so the figures are reproducible rather than taken on trust.

15
00:01:14.553 --> 00:01:18.993
Around this, an organisation gets the controls an examiner looks for.

16
00:01:18.993 --> 00:01:26.265
Policy changes are drafted, simulated against past verdicts, and only go live when a second person approves them.

17
00:01:26.715 --> 00:01:31.399
When a no go must be overridden for a good reason, it goes through an exception.

18
00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:37.488
A reviewer can approve, reject, or ask for more evidence first, and the decision stays with the verdict.

19
00:01:37.938 --> 00:01:40.422
Investigations keep a hash-chained log.

20
00:01:40.422 --> 00:01:46.663
Each entry carries the fingerprint of the one before, so nothing can be quietly edited or removed.

21
00:01:47.113 --> 00:01:54.025
Signed webhooks push events to your own systems, and the Compliance API gives them read access to verdicts and readings.

22
00:01:55.725 --> 00:01:56.647
It starts free.

23
00:01:56.647 --> 00:02:01.933
Pro gives a desk every screen, at seven hundred forty-nine dollars per seat per month.

24
00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:09.930
Institutional covers regulated teams with unlimited seats and the organisation features, at four thousand dollars a month.

25
00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:14.693
Enterprise and Strategic start at one hundred twenty thousand dollars a year.

26
00:02:15.143 --> 00:02:16.597
NOSHASHI is in beta.

27
00:02:16.597 --> 00:02:20.379
It gives information, not financial or legal advice.

28
00:02:20.379 --> 00:02:24.743
Current details are on the pricing page at noshashi dot app.
